      "name": "RoutingPolicy",
      "line_number": 77,
      "docstring": "Minimal routing policy used by L2 cognitive agents.\n\nFields:\n    default_model: fallback model for unspecified tasks.\n    strategy_model: model used for strategy generation.\n    drafting_model: model used for draft generation.\n    qa_model: model used for QA checks.\n    safety_model: model used for safety evaluation.\n    tot_branch_count: Tree-of-Thought branching factor.",
      "imports": [],
      "dependencies": [],
      "responsibility_level": "L5",
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "node_type": "function",
      "name": "build_routing_policy",
      "line_number": 102,
      "docstring": "Construct a RoutingPolicy based on ComplexityLevel and optional meta_profile.\n\nRules:\n    LOW complexity -> light models, 2 branches.\n    MEDIUM complexity -> standard models, 3 branches.\n    HIGH complexity -> heavy models, 5 branches.\n\nIf meta_profile contains bias overrides, they are applied here.",
      "imports": [],
      "dependencies": [
        "hasattr",
        "RoutingPolicy"
      ],
      "responsibility_level": "L5",
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "node_type": "function",
      "name": "select_model_for_task",
      "line_number": 161,
      "docstring": "Return the model name for a given task using the policy.\n\nTasks: \"strategy\", \"drafting\", \"qa\", \"safety\", or fallback to default.\n\nIf a council vote is provided and has a model override, use it.",
